<title>NETHERLANDS: ABN AMRO Chicago sets US$ 400 mln 7.30 pct bond.</title>
<headline>ABN AMRO Chicago sets US$ 400 mln 7.30 pct bond.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following issue was announced by ABN AMRO's Chicago branch:</p>
<p> BORROWER ABN AMRO</p>
<p> AMT US$ 400 MLN	COUPON 7.30	    MATURITY 2006/2026</p>
<p> TYPE SUBORDINATED    ISS PRICE 97.79	PAY DATE 01.06.97</p>
<p> LAST MOODY Aa2	 REOFFER  =	     PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p> LAST S&amp;P AA</p>
<p>Note: ABN Amro said the issue would be redeemed at par on Dec 1, 2026, or, at the option of the Chicago Branch and subject to approval from the Dutch Central Bank, on Dec 1, 2006.</p>
</text>
